## Quality checks

AI agents default to running backend commands inside the Compose `web` service,
unless you choose the local UV workflow. The generated `AGENTS.md` links to focused guidance in
`docs/agent-instructions/`, including the development conventions and full
completion checklist.

For Docker development, build the image with `docker compose build`, then run:

```shell
docker compose run --rm web uv sync --locked
docker compose run --rm web uv lock --check
docker compose run --rm web uv run ruff check .
docker compose run --rm web uv run ruff format --check .
docker compose run --rm web uv run python scripts/check_django_templates.py
docker compose run --rm web uv run python manage.py check
docker compose run --rm web uv run python manage.py makemigrations --check --dry-run
docker compose run --rm web uv run python manage.py test
```

For local development, `make check` runs lint, formatting checks, and Django's
test suite. Also check the lockfile, system configuration, and missing migrations:

```shell
make check
uv lock --check
{% if database != "sqlite3" %}DATABASE_HOST=127.0.0.1 {% endif %}uv run python manage.py check
{% if database != "sqlite3" %}DATABASE_HOST=127.0.0.1 {% endif %}uv run python manage.py makemigrations --check --dry-run
```

{% if database != "sqlite3" %}Start the database with `make database` first. Direct local Django commands need
the database credentials and port from `.env` exported in your shell; the Make
targets load `.env` themselves.

{% endif %}The Git hooks below run on the host using UV, including during Docker development.

Initialize version control and install the hooks after generation. Pre-commit's
`--all-files` option means all files known to Git, so the initial `git add` is
required:

```shell
git init
git add --all
uv run pre-commit install
uv run pre-commit run --all-files
```

If a formatter changes files during that first run, inspect the changes and run
`git add --all` again before committing.

Use `uv add` and `uv remove` for dependencies. `pyproject.toml` and `uv.lock` are
authoritative; this project intentionally does not use `requirements.txt`.
